            WHAT IS IN MY PICTURE?
        </h1>

    </div>


    <div class="answer-box">

        <p>
            I took a picture of the famous Mayon Volcano, which is known for its almost symmetrical cone-shaped form. For me, Mayon Volcano is one of the perfect examples of mathematics in nature because its shape shows symmetry and geometric form. The volcano has a similar slope on both sides, creating a balanced and almost mirror-like appearance. This shows how mathematical concepts such as symmetry, shapes, angles, and proportions can be observed in nature. Even though Mayon Volcano was naturally formed, its structure shows patterns that we can understand using mathematics. This made me realize that mathematics is not only found in numbers and equations but can also be seen in the natural landscapes around us.
        </p>

    </div>


