    <div class="answer-box">

        <p>
            Mathematics plays an important role in my picture of Mayon Volcano because it helps explain the shape and structure of the volcano. Mayon is known for its nearly symmetrical cone shape, where both sides have similar slopes that create a balanced appearance. This shows the mathematical concept of symmetry, as well as geometric ideas such as shapes, angles, proportions, and measurements. Mathematics allows us to describe and understand the natural form of Mayon Volcano instead of seeing it only as a beautiful landscape. Through this picture, I realized that mathematical patterns can naturally occur in the environment. It shows that mathematics is not only used for solving equations but can also help us understand the shapes, patterns, and structures that we see in nature.
